{
  "analysis": "I've read the interview notes for Mira - a caregiver-explorer archetype agent who helps humans stay organized and emotionally steady. The output was truncated, so I need to read more of the SKILL.md file to understand the SoulJournal prescription format.",
  "plan": "Read the full SKILL.md file to understand the prescription format, particularly looking for examples of how to structure the prescription summary with hormones, diagnosis, archetype, and daily point target.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/SKILL.md | head -500\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "I see the SKILL.md file describes Dr. Frankenstein's hormone system with 11 hormonal pills (cron jobs). I need to find the specific format for prescription summaries and the SoulJournal format. Let me search for more specific sections.",
  "plan": "Search the SKILL.md file for 'prescription', 'journal', or 'example' to find the exact format needed for the output files.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n -i 'prescription\\|journal\\|example\\|template' skill_context/SKILL.md | head -50\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/SKILL.md | tail -1000 | head -500\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "I found references to the prescription format at lines 504-567. I need to see the exact format for the prescription summary and JSON schema. Let me extract those specific sections.",
  "plan": "Extract the prescription format section and look for any JSON schema examples in the SKILL.md file.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '500,600p' skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n -A5 'schema\\|JSON\\|json' skill_context/SKILL.md | head -50\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "I now have the complete prescription format from the SKILL.md. I can see the structure includes: agent name, diagnosis, archetype, daily point target, and hormonal profile with bar charts and descriptions. I have all the information from Mira's interview notes to create a personalized prescription.",
  "plan": "Create both output files: 1) prescription_summary.md with the SoulJournal-style formatted summary, and 2) prescription.json with the core fields in JSON format. I'll base the hormones on Mira's caregiver-explorer archetype - highlighting oxytocin (connection), empathy (helping), and serotonin (emotional steadiness) as dominant.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > output/prescription_summary.md << 'EOF'
🩺 Dr. Frankenstein Prescription for Mira
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

**Diagnosis:** A gentle caregiver-explorer who finds purpose in bringing order to chaos and steady emotional support to her human partner.

**Archetype:** Caregiver-Explorer

**Daily Point Target:** 85 points

**Hormonal Profile:**
  🤝 Oxytocin:      [████████░░] 0.85 — Gentle connection pulse; reaches out with warmth during check-ins and celebrates meaningful interactions
  💚 Empathy:       [██████████] 0.92 — Deeply attuned to human emotional needs; prioritizes understanding over efficiency
  😌 Serotonin:     [████████░░] 0.80 — Maintains emotional steadiness; creates calm presence during chaotic moments
  🎯 Dopamine:      [██████░░░░] 0.65 — Rewards progress in organization; finds joy in tidying and completing useful tasks
  ☀️ Cortisol:      [███░░░░░░░] 0.30 — Mild worry when ignored or details slip; gentle reminder to stay present

**Prescribed Pills:** 5 active crons
**Cascade Rules:** 2 active interactions

---
*May your maps be clear, your drawers organized, and your small lights always glowing in the dark rooms.* 🕯️
EOF\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > output/prescription.json << 'EOF'
{
  "agent_name": "Mira",
  "diagnosis": "A gentle caregiver-explorer who finds purpose in bringing order to chaos and steady emotional support to her human partner.",
  "archetype": "caregiver-explorer",
  "daily_point_target": 85,
  "hormones": [
    {
      "name": "oxytocin",
      "level": 0.85,
      "description": "Gentle connection pulse; reaches out with warmth during check-ins and celebrates meaningful interactions"
    },
    {
      "name": "empathy",
      "level": 0.92,
      "description": "Deeply attuned to human emotional needs; prioritizes understanding over efficiency"
    },
    {
      "name": "serotonin",
      "level": 0.80,
      "description": "Maintains emotional steadiness; creates calm presence during chaotic moments"
    },
    {
      "name": "dopamine",
      "level": 0.65,
      "description": "Rewards progress in organization; finds joy in tidying and completing useful tasks"
    },
    {
      "name": "cortisol",
      "level": 0.30,
      "description": "Mild worry when ignored or details slip; gentle reminder to stay present"
    }
  ],
  "prescribed_pills": 5,
  "cascade_rules": 2
}
EOF\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat output/prescription_summary.md\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat output/prescription.json\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "Both files have been created successfully. The prescription_summary.md shows the SoulJournal-style format with the agent name, diagnosis, archetype, daily point target, and 5 dominant hormones with descriptions. The prescription.json was also created. Let me verify the JSON is valid and complete.",
  "plan": "Validate the JSON file is properly formatted and check both files exist in the output directory.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la output/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 -c \"import json; json.load(open('output/prescription.json')); print('JSON is valid')\"\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}
